{"step_index":4145,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T22:44:44Z","thinking":"Investigating text normalization routines within the codebase. The `normalize_text` function in the text matching module omits specific character normalizations crucial for accurate matching, especially with Arabic script variations. There's a separate `normalize_for_search` function, which suggests an attempt at enhanced normalization, likely for a specific application. It's important to understand the differences and intended use cases for each function.\n\n\nThe `normalize_for_search` function's digit and character replacement logic appears incomplete, missing Farsi characters and digits, potentially hindering accurate Arabic and Persian text matching. The `extract_form_group` function's reliance on `normalize_text` without punctuation removal leads to incorrect word splitting, impacting form group identification. Further analysis of stop words used in the search function is required, focusing on normalization to ensure consistent search results, specifically in scenarios involving character variations.\n\n\nIdentified that specific words were not being treated as stopwords during similarity comparisons, leading to lower match scores. Investigating ways to incorporate these findings, along with the observed variations, into the prompt. Focusing on prompt adjustments to improve future matches based on character variations and stopword treatment. Testing modifications within a dedicated test environment, without altering core application files or the user's output.\n\n\nNormalization routines are being enhanced by adding Farsi/Urdu character replacements and Eastern digit normalization within the text matching and search modules, addressing previous shortcomings. Punctuation handling in form group extraction will be improved, substituting punctuation with spaces, which will prevent incorrect word splitting. Further, new metadata descriptors were incorporated into the stop word list to refine brand extraction.\n\nPrompt adjustments are underway, with the initial focus on refining the OCR tolerance rule to encompass broader spelling variations, phonetic transliterations, and OCR errors. All these changes are tested in a controlled environment to ensure no adverse impact on the existing application.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"import sys\nsys.path.insert(0, '.')\nimport re\nfrom rapidfuzz import fuzz\n\ndef normalize_enhanced(text: str) -> str:\n    if not text:\n        return \"\"\n    text = str(text).lower()\n    text = re.sub(r'[\\u064B-\\u065F\\u0670\\u0640]', '', text)\n    text = re.sub(r'[أإآٱ]', 'ا', text)\n    text = re.sub(r'ة', 'ه', text)\n    text = re.sub(r'[ىي\\u06CC]', 'ي', text)  # Arabic Yeh, Alef Maqsura, Farsi Yeh\n    text = text.replace('\\u06A9', 'ك')       # Farsi Keheh\n    text = text.replace('\\u067E', 'ب')       # Farsi Peh\n    text = text.replace('\\u06C0', 'ه').replace('\\u06C1', 'ه')\n    for e, w in zip('٠١٢٣٤٥٦٧٨٩۰۱۲۳۴۵۶۷۸۹', '01234567890123456789'):\n        text = text.replace(e, w)\n    text = re.sub(r'[^\\w\\s]', ' ', text)\n    text = re.sub(r'\\s+', ' ', text).strip()\n    return text\n\n# Test 1: Durafos with Farsi Yeh\ns1 = \"ديورافوس 1 امبول\"\nw1 = \"دیورافس امول = دیور فوس\"\nn_s1 = normalize_enhanced(s1)\nn_w1 = normalize_enhanced(w1)\nprint(\"Test 1 - Durafos:\")\nprint(\"  n_s1:\", n_s1)\nprint(\"  n_w1:\", n_w1)\nprint(\"  token_sort_ratio:\", fuzz.token_sort_ratio(n_s1, n_w1))\n\n# Test 2: Levanox form extraction with slash\nfrom src.fast_match.search import FORM_GROUPS\n\ndef extract_form_group_enhanced(text: str) -> str | None:\n    text = re.sub(r'(\\d+)', r' \\1 ', str(text))\n    text = re.sub(r'[^\\w\\s]', ' ', text)\n    norm = normalize_enhanced(text)\n    words = set(norm.split())\n    for group_name, group_words in FORM_GROUPS.items():\n        if words & group_words:\n            return group_name\n    return None\n\nf_req = extract_form_group_enhanced(\"ليفانوكس2شريط س ج\")\nf_wh = extract_form_group_enhanced(\"ليفانوكس كبسول/باكت 200\")\nprint(\"\\nTest 2 - Levanox Form:\")\nprint(\"  Req form:\", f_req)\nprint(\"  Wh form :\", f_wh)\nprint(\"  Forms compatible?\", f_req == f_wh)\n\n# Test 3: Vental with stopwords\nEXTRA_STOPWORDS = {'عادي', 'عادى', 'مركب'}\nPHARMA_STOPWORDS = {\n    'اقراص', 'قرص', 'كبسول', 'كبسوله', 'كبسولات', 'حبوب', 'شراب', 'شرب', 'معلق', 'سائل',\n    'مرهم', 'كريم', 'جل', 'جيل', 'امبول', 'امبوله', 'امبولات', 'حقن', 'فيال',\n    'لبوس', 'لبوسة', 'لبوسه', 'تحاميل', 'اقماع', 'نقط', 'قطرة', 'قطره',\n    'بخاخ', 'بخاخة', 'بخاخه', 'سبراي', 'فوار', 'اكياس', 'كيس',\n    'شامبو', 'غسول', 'صابون', 'صابونة', 'صابونه', 'محلول', 'مس', 'دهان', 'فيلم', 'شريط',\n    'مجم', 'جم', 'جرام', 'مل', 'مللي', 'لتر', 'ميكرو', 'علبه', 'علبة',\n    'باكت', 'باكو', 'كرتونه', 'كرتونة', 'فلتر',\n    'س', 'ج', 'سعر', 'جديد', 'قديم', 'تاريخ', 'بعيد', 'قريب', 'صغير', 'كبير', 'وسط',\n    'محلي', 'مستورد', 'خاص', 'نقدى', 'اجل'\n} | EXTRA_STOPWORDS\n\ndef extract_brand_enhanced(text: str) -> str:\n    text = re.sub(r'(\\d+)', r' \\1 ', text)\n    text = re.sub(r'[^\\w\\s]', ' ', text)\n    norm = normalize_enhanced(text)\n    words = [w for w in norm.split() if w not in PHARMA_STOPWORDS and not w.isdigit() and len(w) > 1]\n    return \" \".join(words)\n\nb_vental_req = extract_brand_enhanced(\"فنتال بخاخ العربية\")\nb_vental_wh = extract_brand_enhanced(\"فتال عادى بخاخ\")\nprint(\"\\nTest 3 - Vental Brand:\")\nprint(\"  Req brand:\", b_vental_req)\nprint(\"  Wh brand :\", b_vental_wh)\nprint(\"  Ratio:\", fuzz.ratio(\"فنتال\", \"فتال\"))\n","Description":"Test enhanced normalization, form extraction, and brand extraction","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\scratch\\test_improvements.py","toolAction":"Write test script","toolSummary":"Test enhancements"}}]}
